<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n106296" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ὑδᾰτ-ίς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ίδος</span>,
			ἡ, in pl., <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b>
				=
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">σταγόνες</span>
			, <i><span class="en">
				Hsch.
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Phot.
			</span></i>; as a urinary disease, <i><span class="en">
				Cael.Aur.
				<u>TP</u>
				5.4
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>II.</b>
			<i>watery vesicle, hydatid,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Sor.
				1.58
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Gal.
				18(2).679
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				<u>UP</u>
				10.7
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>III.</b>
			<i>a disease in the liver,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Id.
				18(1).165
			</span></i>: also <i>in the hoofs of horses,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Hippiatr.
				77
			</span></i>. </div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense2"><b>IV.</b>
			<i>a gem,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Mart.Cap.
				1.75
			</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
    <div class="alpheios-lex-alph-source">From <u>
            <u>A Greek-English Lexicon</u>
        </u> (Henry George Liddell, Robert Scott, Oxford, Clarendon Press, 1940) </div>
